---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import ResizableDemo from "../../components/ResizableDemo";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<Docs
  title="Resizable"
  description="Panels split by a draggable, keyboard-friendly divider, with saved sizes."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Resizable</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    Panels that share a row or a column, split by a divider people can drag or
    move with the keyboard. Sizes can be limited and remembered between visits.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8"><ResizableDemo client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Resizable usage"
      code={`import {
  ResizableHandle,
  ResizablePanel,
  ResizablePanelGroup,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/resizable";

<div className="h-64 rounded-lg border">
  <ResizablePanelGroup orientation="horizontal">
    <ResizablePanel defaultSize="28%" minSize="220px">
      <FileTree />
    </ResizablePanel>
    <ResizableHandle aria-label="Resize file tree" />
    <ResizablePanel minSize="35%">
      <OpenFile />
    </ResizablePanel>
  </ResizablePanelGroup>
</div>`}
    />
    <p>
      The group fills its parent, so give the parent a height. <code
        >orientation</code
      > is <code>"horizontal"</code> (default), which places panels side by side,
      or <code>"vertical"</code>, which stacks them. Panels and handles must be
      direct children of the group. Fragments are fine.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>defaultSize</code>, <code>minSize</code>, and <code>maxSize</code> take
      a percent such as <code>"40%"</code>, or a length in <code>px</code>, <code
        >rem</code
      >, <code>em</code>, <code>vw</code>, or <code>vh</code>. A plain number is
      pixels. A string without a unit is a percent. Panels without a <code
        >defaultSize</code
      > share the space that is left. A <code>px</code> minimum is checked again when
      the group changes size.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Handle</h2>
    <p>
      <code>ResizableHandle</code> draws a 1px line with a 9px hit area (24px on touch
      screens). Add <code>withHandle</code> for a small grip on splits people resize
      often, like a chat and its canvas. Leave it off for quiet splits like a file
      tree. Always give the handle an <code>aria-label</code> that names what it resizes.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Saved layouts</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Saved layout usage"
      code={`import { useResizableLayout } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/resizable";

const layout = useResizableLayout({
  id: "app:chat-canvas",
  panelIds: open ? ["chat", "canvas"] : ["chat"],
  onlySaveAfterUserInteractions: true,
});

<ResizablePanelGroup
  defaultLayout={layout.defaultLayout}
  onLayoutChanged={layout.onLayoutChanged}
>
  <ResizablePanel id="chat" minSize="40%" defaultSize={open ? "55%" : "100%"}>
    <Chat />
  </ResizablePanel>
  {open && (
    <>
      <ResizableHandle withHandle aria-label="Resize canvas" />
      <ResizablePanel id="canvas" minSize="320px" defaultSize="45%">
        <Canvas />
      </ResizablePanel>
    </>
  )}
</ResizablePanelGroup>`}
    />
    <p>
      A layout is panel sizes in percent, keyed by panel <code>id</code>. <code
        >defaultLayout</code
      > is used when it names every panel shown. Otherwise each panel's <code
        >defaultSize</code
      > applies. When panels are added or removed, the layout starts again from the
      defaults or the saved layout for that set of panels.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>onLayoutChange</code> runs on every change, including each pointer move.
      <code>onLayoutChanged</code> runs once a change settles, with <code
        >{"{ isUserInteraction }"}</code
      >. <code>useResizableLayout</code> saves to <code>localStorage</code> by default,
      or to any <code>storage</code> with <code>getItem</code> and <code
        >setItem</code
      >. With <code>onlySaveAfterUserInteractions</code>, it only saves sizes a
      person chose.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The handle is a focusable <code>role="separator"</code> with <code
        >aria-valuenow</code
      >, <code>aria-valuemin</code>, and <code>aria-valuemax</code> for the panel
      before it, and <code>aria-controls</code> pointing at that panel. Arrow keys
      along the split move it 5%. Home and End move it to that panel's minimum and
      maximum. Right-to-left pages flip the horizontal keys and drag.
    </p>
    <p>
      Line and grip colors change in 120ms and stop when reduced motion is
      requested. While dragging, the page keeps a resize cursor and text is not
      selected.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      The line uses <code>--sprout-line</code>, <code>--sprout-border</code> on hover,
      and <code>--sprout-focus</code> while focused or dragging. The grip uses <code
        >--sprout-border</code
      > and <code>--sprout-border-strong</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
